  "question": {
    "text": "A solid sphere of radius&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></math> is gently placed on a rough horizontal surface with an initial angular speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">ω</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;but no linear velocity. If the coefficient of friction is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">μ</mi></math>, then the time&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></math> when the slipping will stop is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0022_7c69f5d55063.jpg\" style=\"width: 281px; height: 158px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <mn>2</mn> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>7</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> <mfrac> <mrow> <mtext>r</mtext> <msub> <mtext>ω</mtext> <mn>0</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mtext>μ</mtext> <mtext>g</mtext> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </math>",
